# Line endings.
#
# The pipeline writes its output with an explicit "\n", and both CI and
# `cmp` assert that rebuilding produces a byte-identical file. On a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true git would rewrite those files to CRLF on
# the way out, so every rebuild would look like a change to the whole file
# and the reproducibility check would never pass locally.
*           text=auto eol=lf

# Except the roster CSVs. Python's csv module writes \r\n by definition
# (RFC 4180), so these are CRLF on disk and normalising them would produce a
# diff on every `fetch`.
*.csv       text eol=crlf

# Generated. Collapse them in review; they are the build's output, not
# something anyone edits.
candidate_profiles_site/data/profiles.js  linguist-generated=true -diff
candidate_profiles_site/data/geo.js       linguist-generated=true -diff

# Vendored, not generated: the us-atlas 10m state boundaries, already
# projected. Nobody reviews 82 KB of coordinates, so keep it out of diffs,
# but it is a source input rather than build output.
us_atlas_states_topo.json                 linguist-vendored=true -diff

*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
